      "side": 1,
      "message": "For locally built jars, soong makes sure the shell script always has a newer timestamp than the jar.  For prebuilt jars maybe we should manually add a dependency on the jar, or skip the shell script and execute java directly?\n\nIf a new version of the tool might result in a different output file contents then we should have a dependency.  That will keep incremental builds 100% reproducible and reliable.  Other than parsing time, the cost in ninja should be very small - it internally builds a build graph, then stats each node once, so it will only have to stat the proguard jar once.\n\nThe dependency on ccache is less useful, since a new version of ccache shouldn\u0027t result in a different output file, but I left the dependency in because ccache should fast if only the ccache binary has changed.  I\u0027d be fine with removing it.",
